Co-authored-by: optout <13562139+optout21@users.noreply.github.com>

12f691cf28 validation: return block-file flush errors

Return before writing block-index metadata or coins data when the block or undo file flush fails in FlushStateToDisk().
Keep the last-flushed marker and on-disk coins tip at the previous successful flush.
The lower layer already reports the specific error through flushError().

This stops subsequent writes in the failing invocation. Later flushes can retry and write if they succeed, including during shutdown.
ConnectTip() and DisconnectTip() propagate the error before updating the chain tip, after applying the block's coins changes in memory.
</commits>

